IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpa-types`
IMPORT `cpa-schedules`

-- Carbon Pricing Act 2018 — GOAL 1: MUST THIS PERSON REGISTER, OR MAY IT
-- DEREGISTER? and GOAL 2: WHAT MUST IT REPORT, AND BY WHEN?
--
-- Parts 1 to 4: what a business facility is and who controls it (ss 3-5),
-- registration and deregistration (ss 7-10), emissions reports, verification
-- and monitoring plans (ss 11-15), and the saving for 2019 (s 79).
--
-- Source: ../source/CPA2018.txt.

§ `Goals 1 and 2 — registration and reporting`

§§ `The period this encoding states the law for`

-- The text is consolidated as at 6 Oct 2026. Act 37 of 2022, in force
-- 1 January 2024, rewrote registration (s 7(1A), (5)-(7), s 8(1)(a)(ii),
-- (4)(b)), reporting periods (s 11(2A)-(2D)), the tax (s 16(1A), (4)) and
-- payment (Part 5 Divisions 1A, 3-6). The earlier text was not supplied, so
-- an emissions year or event before 2024 refuses (FORK F1).
@ref Act 37 of 2022; Legislative History item 7
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law is encoded for the year` year MEANS
    IF   year LESS THAN 2024
    THEN REFUSE "the Act as it stood before the Carbon Pricing (Amendment) Act 2022 (in force 1 January 2024) is not encoded"
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `What a business facility is, and who controls it (ss 3-5)`

-- s 3(1): "A business facility is a single site at which any business activity
-- is carried out." s 3(3): activities on more than one parcel are at a single
-- site "if the same person has operational control over the business activity,
-- and — (a) the parcels of land are contiguous, adjacent or adjoining, or
-- separated only by any road or pathway ..., or drain or waterway; or (b) where
-- paragraph (a) does not apply, there is a dependency between the activities
-- ..., having regard to any circumstances prescribed."
@ref s 3(1), (3)
GIVEN f IS A `Site facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carried out at a single site:` f IF
        NOT f's `carried out on more than one parcel of land`
    OR  (    f's `the same person has operational control over the activity`
         AND (    "(a)" ... f's `parcels contiguous, adjacent, adjoining, or separated only by a road, pathway, drain or waterway`
              OR  "(b)" ... f's `a prescribed dependency between the activities on the parcels`))

-- s 4(1): a person has operational control if it may introduce and implement
-- "one or more of" operating, health and safety, or environmental policies.
-- s 4(2): "Only one person can have operational control ... at any one time."
-- s 4(3): if more than one qualifies, "the person that has the greatest
-- authority" does. The Act gives no answer for a tie at the greatest.
@ref s 4
GIVEN candidates IS A LIST OF `Policy authority`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the person with operational control among` candidates MEANS
    CONSIDER `qualifying`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF   count (filter (GIVEN x YIELD x's `rank of authority` EQUALS `the greatest`) `qualifying`) GREATER THAN 1
        THEN REFUSE "s 4(3): two or more persons share the greatest authority, and s 4(2) allows only one"
        ELSE JUST (`the one with` `the greatest`)
    WHERE
        `qualifying` MEANS filter (GIVEN x YIELD    x's `may introduce and implement operating policies`
                                                 OR x's `may introduce and implement health and safety policies`
                                                 OR x's `may introduce and implement environmental policies`) candidates
        `the greatest` MEANS `the largest of` (map (GIVEN x YIELD x's `rank of authority`) `qualifying`)
        `the largest of` ns MEANS
            CONSIDER ns
            WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
            WHEN n FOLLOWED BY rest THEN IF null rest THEN n ELSE (IF n GREATER THAN `the largest of` rest THEN n ELSE `the largest of` rest)
        `the one with` r MEANS
            CONSIDER filter (GIVEN x YIELD x's `rank of authority` EQUALS r) `qualifying`
            WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x's `person`
            WHEN EMPTY THEN ""

-- s 5(1): "This Act applies only to industry sectors prescribed." s 74: the
-- Minister may exempt a facility or person by order — an input.
@ref s 5(1), s 74
GIVEN f IS A `Site facts`
      `exempted by order under s 74` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the facility:` f `, exempted:` `exempted by order under s 74` IF
        f's `in a prescribed industry sector`
    AND NOT `exempted by order under s 74`

§§ `Goal 1a — registration on reaching a threshold (ss 7(1)-(4), 8)`

DECLARE `Applications required` HAS
    `to be registered as a registered person`             IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(1)(a), (5)(c)
    `to register the facility as a reportable facility`   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(1)(b), (5)(d)
    `to register the facility as a taxable facility`      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 7(1)(c), (5)(d)
    `no later than`                                       IS A MAYBE DATE -- s 8(1)(a)
    `registration in force from`                          IS A MAYBE DATE -- s 8(4)

-- s 7(1): where the reckonable emissions of a facility attain the first
-- emissions threshold in a year (the trigger year), the person with
-- operational control on 31 December of that year (s 7(1A)) must apply (a)
-- to be a registered person, (b) to register the facility as a reportable
-- facility, and (c) if they also attain the second threshold, to register it
-- as a taxable facility. (2): (a) does not apply if the person is already
-- registered, or if the facility "will cease to be under the operational
-- control of the person by the time the person must make the application".
-- (3), (4): (b) and (c) do not apply if already so registered.
-- s 8(1)(a)(i): "no later than 30 June of the year immediately after the
-- trigger year"; s 8(4)(a): in force "starting on 1 January of the year
-- immediately after the trigger year".
@ref ss 7(1)-(4), 8(1)(a)(i), 8(4)(a)
GIVEN `trigger year`        IS A NUMBER
      `reckonable tCO2e`    IS A NUMBER
      status                IS A `Registration status`
      `control will cease before the application is due` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Applications required`
`the applications required for the year` `trigger year` `, reckonable tCO2e` `reckonable tCO2e` `, status` status `, control ceasing:` `control will cease before the application is due` MEANS
    IF NOT `the law is encoded for the year` `trigger year`
    THEN REFUSE "no source is encoded for this year"
    ELSE `Applications required` WITH
            `to be registered as a registered person`           IS `(a)`
            `to register the facility as a reportable facility` IS `(b)`
            `to register the facility as a taxable facility`    IS `(c)`
            `no later than`                                     IS (IF `any` THEN JUST (YMD (`trigger year` PLUS 1) 6 30) ELSE NOTHING)
            `registration in force from`                        IS (IF `any` THEN JUST (YMD (`trigger year` PLUS 1) 1 1) ELSE NOTHING)
    WHERE
        `triggered` MEANS `reckonable tCO2e` AT LEAST `the first emissions threshold`
        `(a)` MEANS     `triggered`
                    AND NOT "(2)(a)" ... status's `a registered person`
                    AND NOT "(2)(b)" ... `control will cease before the application is due`
        `(b)` MEANS `triggered` AND NOT "(3)" ... status's `registered as a reportable facility of the person`
        `(c)` MEANS     `triggered`
                    AND `reckonable tCO2e` AT LEAST `the second emissions threshold`
                    AND NOT "(4)" ... status's `registered as a taxable facility of the person`
        `any` MEANS `(a)` OR `(b)` OR `(c)`

§§ `Goal 1b — registration on a transfer of operational control (ss 7(5)-(7), 8)`

-- s 7(5): where X (a registered person of the facility, or the person with
-- control on 31 December of a trigger year) transfers operational control to
-- Y, Y must apply (c) to be a registered person (unless already one, (6)),
-- and (d) to register the facility "as a reportable facility or as both a
-- reportable facility and a taxable facility (as the case may be)".
-- FORK F2: "as the case may be" is read from the deadlines in s 8(1)(a)(ii),
-- which provide for Y's taxable registration in cases (B) and (C): Y registers
-- the facility as taxable where it was a taxable facility of X, or where its
-- reckonable emissions attained the second threshold in the year before the
-- transfer.
-- s 8(1)(a)(ii): "(A) if, in the year immediately before the year of the
-- transfer, the total amount of reckonable GHG emissions ... does not attain
-- the second emissions threshold — no later than 30 June of the year
-- immediately after the year of the transfer; (B) if — (BA) ... not
-- registered as a taxable facility of X; and (BB) [the previous year's
-- emissions attain the second threshold], no later than the later of ...
-- (BC) 30 June of the year of the transfer; (BD) 30 days after the date of
-- the transfer; and (C) if ... registered as a taxable facility of X — no
-- later than 30 days after the date of the transfer". s 8(4)(b): in force from
-- the date of the transfer.
@ref ss 7(5)-(7), 8(1)(a)(ii), 8(4)(b)
GIVEN t                       IS A `Transfer of control`
      `Y is already a registered person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Applications required`
`the applications Y must make on the transfer` t `, Y already registered:` `Y is already a registered person` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the law is encoded for the year` (DATE_YEAR (t's `date of transfer`))
              THEN REFUSE "no source is encoded for this year"
           IF NOT t's `X was a registered person of the facility, or had control on 31 December of a trigger year`
              THEN `Applications required` WITH
                      `to be registered as a registered person`           IS FALSE
                      `to register the facility as a reportable facility` IS FALSE
                      `to register the facility as a taxable facility`    IS FALSE
                      `no later than`                                     IS NOTHING
                      `registration in force from`                        IS NOTHING
           OTHERWISE `Applications required` WITH
                      `to be registered as a registered person`           IS NOT `Y is already a registered person`   -- (5)(c), (6)
                      `to register the facility as a reportable facility` IS TRUE                                    -- (5)(d)
                      `to register the facility as a taxable facility`    IS `taxable for Y`                         -- (5)(d), F2
                      `no later than`                                     IS JUST `the deadline`
                      `registration in force from`                        IS JUST (t's `date of transfer`)
    WHERE
        `transfer` MEANS t's `date of transfer`
        `previous year at the second threshold` MEANS t's `reckonable tCO2e in the year before the transfer` AT LEAST `the second emissions threshold`
        `taxable for Y` MEANS t's `the facility was registered as a taxable facility of X` OR `previous year at the second threshold`
        `the deadline` MEANS
            BRANCH IF t's `the facility was registered as a taxable facility of X`
                      THEN `transfer` PLUS 30                                                  -- (C)
                   IF `previous year at the second threshold`
                      THEN `the later of` (YMD (DATE_YEAR `transfer`) 6 30) (`transfer` PLUS 30) -- (B)
                   OTHERWISE YMD (DATE_YEAR `transfer` PLUS 1) 6 30                            -- (A)

§§ `Goal 1c — deregistration (ss 9, 10)`

DECLARE `Kind of registration` IS ONE OF
    `as a taxable facility`
    `as a reportable facility`

-- s 9(1) (taxable) and (3) (reportable): the registered person may apply to
-- deregister if "(a) [it] ceases to have operational control ...; (aa) [it]
-- has ceased to operate the business facility and has no intention of
-- resuming its business activity within the next 36 months ...; (b) the total
-- amount of reckonable GHG emissions ... does not attain the [second (taxable)
-- or first (reportable)] emissions threshold for each of 3 consecutive years;
-- or (c) where any modification ... is completed and — (i) [the emissions] in
-- the year in which the modification is completed ... [do] not attain the
-- threshold; and (ii) [are] unlikely to attain the threshold in each of the
-- 2 consecutive years immediately following."
@ref s 9(1), (3)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of registration`
      f IS A `Deregistration facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registered person may apply to deregister the facility` k `:` f IF
        "(a)"  ... f's `ceased to have operational control`
    ..  "(aa)" ... f's `ceased to operate with no intention to resume within 36 months`
    ..  "(b)"  ... (count (f's `reckonable tCO2e in each of the last 3 consecutive years`) EQUALS 3 AND all `under` (f's `reckonable tCO2e in each of the last 3 consecutive years`))
    OR  "(c)"  ... (    f's `a modification was completed`
                    AND `under` (f's `reckonable tCO2e in the year the modification was completed`)
                    AND count (f's `likely tCO2e in each of the next 2 years`) EQUALS 2
                    AND all `under` (f's `likely tCO2e in each of the next 2 years`))
    WHERE
        `threshold` MEANS
            CONSIDER k
            WHEN `as a taxable facility`    THEN `the second emissions threshold`
            WHEN `as a reportable facility` THEN `the first emissions threshold`
        `under` x MEANS x LESS THAN `threshold`

-- s 9(4): a registered person may apply to deregister "as such if there is no
-- longer any business facility registered as a reportable facility". s 9(5):
-- the Agency may deregister on its own if the person "has been wound up or
-- dissolved or has otherwise ceased to exist". s 10(4): "Except where
-- section 9(5) applies, the Agency must not deregister a registered person ...
-- if the registered person has not discharged all obligations and liabilities
-- under this Act".
@ref s 9(4), (5), s 10(4)
GIVEN f IS A `Deregistration facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registered person may be deregistered as such:` f IF
        "s 9(5)" ... f's `wound up, dissolved or otherwise ceased to exist`
    OR  (    "s 9(4)"  ... f's `no reportable facility remains registered to the person`
         AND "s 10(4)" ... f's `all obligations and liabilities under the Act discharged`)

-- s 9(2): "a registered person must give the Agency advance written notice of
-- the date that the operational control ... is to cease, at least 45 days
-- before that date." (Offence: s 54(5).)
@ref s 9(2)
GIVEN `control ceases on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify the Agency, control ceasing on` `control ceases on` MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for the year` (DATE_YEAR `control ceases on`)
    THEN `control ceases on` MINUS 45
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for this year: the Act before the 2022 amendments (in force 1 January 2024) is not encoded"

§§ `Goal 2 — emissions reports, verification and monitoring plans (ss 11-15)`

DECLARE `Reporting duties` HAS
    `an emissions report for the year`                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 11(1)
    `the report must be verified by an accredited external auditor` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 12(1)
    `an approved monitoring plan is required`               IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 13(1)

-- s 11(1): a registered person with operational control "for any part of a
-- year" over a reportable facility must submit an emissions report for that
-- year. s 12(1): where the facility is a taxable facility, the report must be
-- prepared on a monitoring plan (s 13(1)), verified by an accredited external
-- auditor, and accompanied by the auditor's report. s 12(3): not for any part
-- of the period "(a) before the approval of the Agency under section 13 for
-- the monitoring plan; or (b) after the deregistration of the business facility
-- as a taxable facility". s 12(2): the non-reckonable part need not be
-- verified.
@ref ss 11(1), 12(1), (3), 13(1)
GIVEN `controlled for part of the year`  IS A BOOLEAN
      status                             IS A `Registration status`
      `monitoring plan approved`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reporting duties`
`the reporting duties, controlled:` `controlled for part of the year` `, status` status `, plan approved:` `monitoring plan approved` MEANS
    `Reporting duties` WITH
        `an emissions report for the year`                              IS `reportable`
        `the report must be verified by an accredited external auditor` IS `reportable` AND `taxable` AND `monitoring plan approved`
        `an approved monitoring plan is required`                       IS `reportable` AND `taxable`
    WHERE
        `reportable` MEANS     `controlled for part of the year`
                           AND status's `a registered person`
                           AND status's `registered as a reportable facility of the person`
        `taxable` MEANS status's `registered as a taxable facility of the person`

-- s 11(2A): "the reporting period for year R is the whole or the part of year R
-- ... for which the business facility is under the operational control of the
-- registered person". s 11(3): the obligation "arises at the end of the
-- reporting period".
@ref s 11(2A), (3)
GIVEN year              IS A NUMBER
      `control from`    IS A DATE
      `control until`   IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`the reporting period in` year `, control from` `control from` `until` `control until` MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for the year` (year)
    THEN LIST `start`, `end`
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for this year: the Act before the 2022 amendments (in force 1 January 2024) is not encoded"
    WHERE
        `start` MEANS IF `control from` GREATER THAN YMD year 1 1 THEN `control from` ELSE YMD year 1 1
        `end` MEANS
            CONSIDER `control until`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN YMD year 12 31
            WHEN JUST u  THEN IF u LESS THAN YMD year 12 31 THEN u ELSE YMD year 12 31

-- s 15(1): a registered person that discovers an error or omission "must notify
-- the Agency ... within 7 working days after the discovery". FORK F3: "working
-- day" is not defined in the Act; read as a day other than a Saturday, a Sunday
-- or a public holiday, the holidays being an input.
@ref s 15(1)
GIVEN discovered         IS A DATE
      `public holidays`  IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify an error discovered on` discovered `, holidays` `public holidays` MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for the year` (DATE_YEAR discovered)
    THEN `working days after` discovered 7
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for this year: the Act before the 2022 amendments (in force 1 January 2024) is not encoded"
    WHERE
        `a working day` d MEANS     NOT `Weekday of` d EQUALS 0
                                AND NOT `Weekday of` d EQUALS 6
                                AND NOT elem d `public holidays`
        `working days after` d n MEANS
            IF   n AT MOST 0 THEN d
            ELSE IF `a working day` (d PLUS 1)
                 THEN `working days after` (d PLUS 1) (n MINUS 1)
                 ELSE `working days after` (d PLUS 1) n

-- s 13(2): before approving a monitoring plan the Agency MAY direct an external
-- auditor's assessment where "(a) ... specialised technical knowledge is
-- required ...; (b) the Agency disagrees with the registered person on any
-- matter set out in the monitoring plan".
@ref s 13(2)
GIVEN `specialised technical knowledge required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Agency disagrees with the plan`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may direct an external auditor's assessment of the plan, technical:` `specialised technical knowledge required` `, disagreement:` `the Agency disagrees with the plan` IF
        "(a)" ... `specialised technical knowledge required`
    OR  "(b)" ... `the Agency disagrees with the plan`

§§ `Saving for 2019 (s 79)`

-- s 79(1): a corporation registered under the Energy Conservation Act 2012 on
-- 31 December 2018 that submitted a monitoring plan in 2018 is, from 1 January
-- 2019, a registered person, and the activity "both a reportable facility and
-- a taxable facility". s 79(2): one whose reckonable emissions attained
-- 2,000 tCO2e in 2017 and that, on 31 December 2018, still had control and was
-- a registered corporation under that Act, is a registered person with a
-- reportable facility.
@ref s 79(1), (2)
GIVEN `ECA-registered on 31 December 2018`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `submitted a monitoring plan in 2018 under ECA s 26C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reckonable tCO2e in 2017`                     IS A NUMBER
      `still had operational control on 31 December 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Registration status`
`the status from 1 January 2019 under s 79, ECA-registered:` `ECA-registered on 31 December 2018` `, plan in 2018:` `submitted a monitoring plan in 2018 under ECA s 26C` `, 2017 tCO2e` `reckonable tCO2e in 2017` `, control kept:` `still had operational control on 31 December 2018` MEANS
    `Registration status` WITH
        `a registered person`                               IS `(1)` OR `(2)`
        `registered as a reportable facility of the person` IS `(1)` OR `(2)`
        `registered as a taxable facility of the person`    IS `(1)`
    WHERE
        `(1)` MEANS `ECA-registered on 31 December 2018` AND `submitted a monitoring plan in 2018 under ECA s 26C`
        `(2)` MEANS     `reckonable tCO2e in 2017` AT LEAST 2000
                    AND `still had operational control on 31 December 2018`
                    AND `ECA-registered on 31 December 2018`
